How will you make a difference? 
 The Manufacturing Engineer works to sustain continual improvement with business processes using lean manufacturing and other improvement techniques. As a Manufacturing Engineer, you will collect data, analyze outputs, and provide leadership for action to improve safety, quality, and increase overall effectiveness of business processes. In this role, you will utilize your experience and expertise to solve problems, drive process adherence, develop and execute objectives for self and others, and can affect short-term and some long-term business goals.&#xa0;
 &#xa0; 
 What do we want to know about you? 
 Do you have:&#xa0;
 • Bachelor’s, MET, EET, or PLET degree or a high school diploma/GED with at least 6-8 years of experience in manufacturing
• Ability to use Manufacturing Lean principles for area rearrangements, NPI, and problem solving.
• Own Lean transformation inside Building 18 driving toward future state vision
• Willingness to challenge the norm and look for new manufacturing techniques and technologies to improve our products
• Proficient skills in Microsoft Office applications
• Experience with CAD software
• Ability to create production drawings from pre-existing models using model dimensions
• Create new models using pre-existing conditions
• Work hands on with machinery and operators to troubleshoot machine failures, process breakdowns, and quality defect sources on the manufacturing floor
• Strong oral and written communications skills
• Strong interpersonal and leadership skills
• Ability to influence others and lead teams
• Ability to lead initiatives of moderate scope and impact
• Ability to multitask across multiple operational initiatives
• Strong and effective problem identification and solution skills
• Proven analytical and quality/process improvement skills
• Willingness to take on tough challenges and grow professionally
 • Ability to work independently and in a team setting
• Strong change management capabilities
 • undefined
 What will your typical day look like? 
 • Develops, observes, evaluates, and improves manufacturing methods and processes to reduce costs.&#xa0;
• Lead the operational team with a project based continuous improvement mindset, looking for innovative ways to execute production plan
 • Manage various cost accounts and projects associated with expense reductions.&#xa0;
• Review and analysis of space requirements, and workflow, and designs layout of equipment and workspace for maximum efficiency.&#xa0;
• Confers with planning and design staff concerning product design and tooling to ensure efficient production methods.&#xa0;
• Develop and execute process improvement strategies that challenge existing operational paradigms
• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to redesign workflows and introduce innovative manufacturing techniques
• Ability to shift organizational mindset from traditional to progressive manufacturing approaches
• Confers with vendors to determine product specifications and arrange for purchase of equipment, materials, or parts, and evaluates products according to specifications and quality standards.&#xa0;
• Estimates production times, staffing requirements, and related costs to provide information for management decisions.&#xa0;
• Communicate with management, engineering, and other staff regarding manufacturing capabilities, and other considerations to facilitate production processes.&#xa0;
• Applies statistical methods to estimate future manufacturing requirements process changes and improvements.&#xa0;
